				</span></i>
			 (where the 
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄψεσθε</span>
			 may be right): pf.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄπωπα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					6.124
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				21.94
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Emp.
				109
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.37
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				63
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Art.</u>
				1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Carn.</u>
				17
			</span></i>; Trag. and Com., as <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				57
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				6
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Lys.</u>
				1157
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				1225
			</span></i>, never in 
				Att.
			 Prose: plpf.
			3sg.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀπώπει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					21.123
				</span></i>
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀπώπεε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					5.92
				</span></i>
			.<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζ᾽</span>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀπώπεσαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					7.125
				</span></i>
			 :—
				Pass.
			, aor. 1
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὤφθην</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				709
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hec.</u>
				970
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				4.73
			</span></i>, etc. ; opt. (
				Ion.
			) 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀφθείησαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					8.7
				</span></i>
			 ; part.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀφθείς,</span>
			inf.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀφθῆναι,</span>
